admin-analytics-title = Usage analytics
admin-analytics-help = Optional event counts, disabled by default. Only consenting mailbox users contribute fixed screen names. The exporter sends counts from the server and runs no provider scripts in the application; a browser tag, below, is separate. Mail content, addresses, searches, route details and user identifiers are excluded. Browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control override consent.
admin-analytics-collector = Collector configuration
admin-analytics-enabled = Enable optional analytics collection
admin-analytics-provider = Provider
admin-analytics-endpoint = Collector endpoint
admin-analytics-endpoint-help = Use an absolute HTTPS URL ending in /api/send for Umami or /matomo.php for Matomo. Credentials, query parameters and fragments are refused.
admin-analytics-site = Website or site ID
admin-analytics-site-help = Umami uses a website UUID. Matomo uses a positive numeric site ID.
admin-analytics-http = Allow unencrypted HTTP for this collector
admin-analytics-save = Save configuration
admin-analytics-reload = Reload
admin-analytics-saved = Analytics configuration saved.
admin-analytics-counts = Exporter status
admin-analytics-status-label = Status
admin-analytics-status-count = Events
admin-analytics-counts-help = Process-local counts reset when the server restarts. Delivered means the collector accepted the request, not that it retained an event. Unique visitors, client devices and client geography are unavailable; collectors see the exporter connection.
admin-analytics-queued = Queued
admin-analytics-delivered = Accepted by collector
admin-analytics-dropped = Dropped
admin-analytics-private = Private collector destinations
admin-analytics-private-help = Allow a specific host or network only for analytics traffic. Metadata, loopback and link-local addresses remain blocked. Proxy routing still applies. Removing an entry affects future requests.
admin-analytics-destination = Host or network, optionally with port
admin-analytics-allow = Allow destination
admin-analytics-remove = Remove
admin-analytics-ga-help = Sends consented screen counts through the server using Google Analytics 4 Measurement Protocol. No Google scripts or tracking cookies are loaded. Advertising consent is denied. Visitor, session and engagement reporting are not supported.
admin-analytics-ga-global = Google global endpoint
admin-analytics-ga-eu = Google EU collection endpoint
admin-analytics-ga-id = Measurement ID
admin-analytics-ga-secret = Measurement Protocol API secret
admin-analytics-ga-secret-stored = A secret is stored securely. Leave blank to keep it. Changing the endpoint or measurement ID requires a replacement secret.
admin-analytics-ga-secret-needed = Create a Measurement Protocol API secret in your Google Analytics web data stream. The server stores it encrypted and never returns it to this form.
admin-analytics-ga-secret-clear = Remove the stored API secret (disable collection first)

## Browser analytics tag (t63)
admin-analytics-tag-title = Browser analytics tag
admin-analytics-tag-help = Optional. Loads an analytics provider's script in the mail app for users who consented. Unlike the exporter above, the provider's code runs in the browser: it sees the page address, the browser and the user's IP address, and the provider may set its own identifiers.
admin-analytics-tag-scope = Where the tag runs
admin-analytics-tag-scope-consent = Only in the mail app, and only for a signed-in user who agreed to this provider in Settings → Privacy. Withdrawing that consent cuts the page off from the provider at once and reloads it, in every open tab of that browser.
admin-analytics-tag-scope-never = Never loaded in message reader frames, detached composer or reader windows, the admin console, the sign-in page, or a browser that has been used for the admin console. Once loaded, it runs with full access to the mail page, including windows and frames that page opens.
admin-analytics-tag-scope-privacy = Never when the browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, or holds an admin console session.
admin-analytics-tag-scope-consent-own = Users agree to this provider separately from the usage counts above. Changing the provider, or anything that changes the loader this server generates, asks every user again. The provider can still change its own script without that.
admin-analytics-tag-enabled = Load this tag for consenting users
admin-analytics-tag-provider = Tag provider
admin-analytics-tag-custom = Custom tag (other provider)
admin-analytics-tag-site-plausible = Site domain
admin-analytics-tag-site-plausible-help = The domain registered in Plausible, such as mail.example.com.
admin-analytics-tag-site-matomo = Site ID
admin-analytics-tag-site-matomo-help = The positive numeric site ID from Matomo. Cookies are disabled in the generated tag.
admin-analytics-tag-site-umami = Website ID
admin-analytics-tag-site-umami-help = The website UUID from Umami. The generated tag excludes the URL fragment and query.
admin-analytics-tag-site-fathom = Site ID
admin-analytics-tag-site-fathom-help = The Fathom site ID: 4 to 16 capital letters and digits.
admin-analytics-tag-site-posthog = Project API key
admin-analytics-tag-site-posthog-help = The PostHog project API key, starting with phc_. Session recording is turned off in the generated tag.
admin-analytics-tag-site-simple-analytics = Hostname (optional)
admin-analytics-tag-site-simple-analytics-help = The hostname registered in Simple Analytics, if it differs from this server's.
admin-analytics-tag-site-cloudflare = Site token
admin-analytics-tag-site-cloudflare-help = The 32-character token from the Cloudflare Web Analytics site settings.
admin-analytics-tag-host = Provider address
admin-analytics-tag-host-help = The https base URL of a self-hosted instance. Leave blank for the provider's cloud service where one exists.
admin-analytics-tag-region = Region
admin-analytics-tag-region-us = United States cloud
admin-analytics-tag-region-eu = European Union cloud
admin-analytics-tag-preset-note = The server builds this provider's documented tag from the fields above and serves it from this server. Only the provider's documented origins are added to the page's Content Security Policy.
admin-analytics-tag-custom-warning = A custom tag runs with full access to users' webmail pages: it can read messages shown in the app, contacts and drafts, and act as the signed-in user. The admin console shares this address, so it could also reach the admin API of anyone signed in to the console in the same browser; the tag is never served while an admin session cookie is present, but an admin who signs in to the console while a tagged mail tab is open is exposed. Only use code from a provider you trust.
admin-analytics-tag-kind = Custom tag source
admin-analytics-tag-kind-url = Script URL
admin-analytics-tag-kind-inline = JavaScript snippet
admin-analytics-tag-script-url = Script URL
admin-analytics-tag-script-url-help = An https URL. Its origin must be listed under script origins.
admin-analytics-tag-snippet = JavaScript snippet
admin-analytics-tag-snippet-help = Paste the JavaScript only, without script tags. It is stored on the server and served as a file from this server. { $used } of { $max } bytes.
admin-analytics-tag-script-origins = Script origins
admin-analytics-tag-script-origins-help = One per line, such as https://cdn.example.com. Origins the tag loads scripts from. https only; https://*.example.com is allowed, a bare * is not.
admin-analytics-tag-connect-origins = Connection origins
admin-analytics-tag-connect-origins-help = One per line. Origins the tag sends data to with fetch, XMLHttpRequest or sendBeacon.
admin-analytics-tag-img-origins = Image origins
admin-analytics-tag-img-origins-help = One per line. Origins the tag loads tracking pixels from, if any.
admin-analytics-tag-acknowledge = I understand this provider's script runs with full access to users' webmail pages.
admin-analytics-tag-csp = Content Security Policy additions
admin-analytics-tag-csp-help = The mail app's policy gains exactly these sources while the tag is enabled, and only for consenting users. Nothing else changes; unsafe-inline and unsafe-eval are never added.
admin-analytics-tag-csp-incomplete = Complete the fields above to see the additions.
admin-analytics-tag-csp-none = no additions
admin-analytics-tag-served = Served at { $path }
admin-analytics-tag-save = Save browser tag
admin-analytics-tag-saved = Browser tag saved.
admin-analytics-tag-test = Test
admin-analytics-tag-test-tooltip = Check that the tag's script can be fetched, without saving
admin-analytics-tag-test-results = Test results
admin-analytics-tag-test-served = The generated file { $path } ({ $bytes } bytes) is being served.
admin-analytics-tag-test-unsaved = The generated file would be { $path } ({ $bytes } bytes). It is served once this configuration is saved and enabled.
admin-analytics-tag-test-ok = Reachable: { $url } ({ $bytes } bytes, { $type })
admin-analytics-tag-test-failed = Not reachable from the server: { $url } ({ $reason })
admin-analytics-tag-preset-warning = The provider's script runs with full access to users' webmail pages, as a custom tag does: it can read what the app shows and act as the signed-in user. If the provider or its server is compromised, so is every consenting user's mail. Only use a provider you trust.
